def add(n,items,scans,package,lines,words,statement,status,klass,fate,refs,search,calc='',detail='',confidence='high',attribution=None):
    C.append(dict(id=f'C-SA14-{n}',items=[f'SA14-{i}' for i in items],cote=60,scans=scans,lines=[f'MPL_60_{package}_transcription.tex:{lines}'],his_statement=words,statement=statement,status_on_pages=status,computation=(f'scripts/calculations.py; outputs/calculations.txt; {calc}; proof_notes.md' if calc else 'No explicit numerical computation is used; see proof_notes.md for the indicated formal argument and scope check.'),**{'class':klass},fate=fate,fate_date='Publication/circulation dates are recorded in references.bib and literature_notes.md; no handwriting date inferred.',present_status='As of 2026-11-19: '+detail,refs=refs.split(';') if refs else [],confidence=confidence,search_events=search.split(';'),attribution=attribution or ('reused printed Bourbaki text; not attributed to the handwritten author' if n>=452 else 'handwritten mathematical text'),page_status_detail=detail))
add(401,[401],[3],'002-035','9–19','P_f=det(1-ft)=Σ(-1)^i Tr(Λ^if)t^i','For every finite-dimensional endomorphism, the exterior trace expansion equals the determinant.','proof sketched','E','Classical linear algebra; the exact determinant convention is also used in Deligne1973 §10.3. No novel theorem is inferred from the notation.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S01','CALC-01', 'Valid without diagonalizability; independently checked by principal minors and triangularization.')
add(402,[402],[3],'002-035','20–29','Z_f=P_f^{-1}; multiplicativité','The reciprocal determinant has complete symmetric traces as coefficients; exact sequences of endomorphisms give products of characteristic functions.','proof sketched','E','Classical symmetric-function and block-triangular determinant identities; comparison located in Deligne1973 §10.3 and BGT2013 §6.','Deligne1973Constants;BGT2013Endomorphisms','LF-S01','CALC-01','Valid as a formal-series identity with rational left side for finite-dimensional f.')
add(403,[403],[3,5],'002-035','30–32,92–102','(1-at)*(1-bt)=1-abt','Tensor product corresponds to the rational Witt star product; ordinary multiplication corresponds to direct sum.','proof sketched','B','The exact rational-Witt identification is established in K-theory of endomorphisms; BGT2013 §5 equation(5.8) and §6 refer back to Almkvist’s1970s result. This is a later terminology/comparison, not a claim of direct influence.','BGT2013Endomorphisms','LF-S01','CALC-01','Valid; missing star in the multifactor display is a scan alarm.')
add(404,[404,405],[5],'002-035','103–126','λ and σ; cancelled generating identity','Exterior and symmetric operations on virtual endomorphisms satisfy λ_s(-V)=σ_{-s}(V); the reciprocal-P convention transports these operations with the corresponding sign.','corrected by himself later','E','Classical λ-ring identities; rational-Witt formalism in BGT2013 §6 is an exact framework, but the cancelled formula is not retained as a second theorem.','BGT2013Endomorphisms','LF-S01','CALC-01','The surviving exchange at125–126 is read in its chosen convention; the earlier identity at115–119 is explicitly deleted.')
add(405,[406,407],[7],'002-035','163–186','P_checkf=(-t)^n det(f)^-1 P_f(t^-1)','For invertible f, reciprocal determinant and reciprocal L identities hold in K(t); they extend to virtual complexes by alternating rank and determinant.','proof sketched','E','Deligne1973 equations(10.3.4)–(10.3.5) give the exact complex version.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S01','CALC-02','Valid; inversion on unrestricted formal series and an unidentified ε exponent are excluded.')
add(406,[408],[9],'002-035','216–243','detF=ε p^{nρ/2}, ε=±1','For rational pure Frobenius data of weightρ, detF is real of absolute valuep^{nρ/2}; for an arbitrary pure ℓ-adic sheaf the reality conclusion is false.','stated without proof','B','Deligne1974 Theorem1.6 and Deligne1980 Corollary3.3.9 establish rationality/weights for the indicated geometric cohomologies. They do not give this assertion for every pure rank-one ℓ-adic character.','Deligne1974WeilI;Deligne1980WeilII','LF-S02','CALC-03','Conditional motivic assertion retained. The ζ₃ rank-one character is a scope countermodel, not a refutation of rational motive hypotheses.')
add(407,[409],[9],'002-035','221–230','nρ/2 entier','For p prime, a rational determinant with complex absolute valuep^{nρ/2} forces nρ even. For q=p^a the corresponding inference is only anρ even.','stated without proof','E','An elementary valuation consequence of rationality. The geometric input supplying rationality is Deligne1974 Theorem1.6/Deligne1980 Corollary3.3.9.','Deligne1974WeilI;Deligne1980WeilII','LF-S02','CALC-03','Valid under rationality. Rank-one F=√2 overQ₇ is pure weight1 and fails that extra hypothesis, so it checks the exact scope.')
add(408,[410],[9,13,53],'002-035','231–243,370–381','checkE≃E(ρ); on admet','A perfect Frobenius-equivariant coefficient pairingE⊗E→Q_ℓ(-ρ) givesE^∨≃E(ρ); purity alone does not construct it.','stated without proof','C','Poincaré/Lefschetz duality supplies particular geometric pairings; Deligne1974/1980 proves weights, not a universal selfduality of pure sheaves. General motivic polarization/standard-conjecture content is not identified as solved by those papers.','Deligne1974WeilI;Deligne1980WeilII;Jannsen1992Numerical','LF-S02','CALC-03','Treat as an admitted coefficient hypothesis; no broad false verdict is attached to the intended polarized motivic context.')
add(409,[411],[9],'002-035','234–243','L_E(t/p^ρ)','For geometric Frobenius, L_{E(r)}(t)=L_E(p^{-r}t).','proof sketched','E','The convention agrees with Deligne1973 §§8,10 and Laumon1987 §0.9.','Deligne1973Constants;Laumon1987Fourier','LF-S01','CALC-08','Valid; residue degree must be included in a closed-point Euler product.')
add(410,[412,413,438],[11],'002-035','295–320','propre; Rf_*DE=D Rf_*E','Proper duality and the trace formula give the two-object functional equation L_{DE}(t)=(-t)^-χ δ L_E(t^-1).','proof sketched','A','Grothendieck’s Bourbaki279 §§3–5 gives the trace/rationality framework (talkDec1964; publication1966). Deligne1973 §§10.3–10.5 gives explicit determinant/duality formulas. SGA5 circulated1965–1966, published1977; manuscript chronology remains unassigned.','Grothendieck1964Lefschetz;Deligne1973Constants;Illusie2026SGA5','LF-S01','CALC-02','Valid with properness and constructible ℓ-adic finiteness; “compactifiable” was visibly replaced by “propre”.')
add(411,[414],[11,13],'002-035','316–320,347–369','avec les conjectures','For smooth properX and lisse pureE, cohomologyH^i has weightρ+i; the resulting determinant magnitude is p^{(n+ρ)χ/2}.','stated without proof','B','Deligne1980 §§3.3.4–3.3.6 supplies the weight bounds whose equality for smooth properX gives this statement. Rational signs and motivic polarizations remain additional hypotheses.','Deligne1980WeilII','LF-S02','CALC-02','Established for the stated ℓ-adic setting; distinguish this theorem from unresolved standard-conjecture positivity.')
add(412,[415],[13],'002-035','347–369','Σ(-1)^i i b_i=nχ','If b_i=b_{2n-i}, then the weighted alternating sum is nχ, and the paired determinant magnitudes give the exponent written on13.','proof sketched','E','Elementary paired-sum identity; cohomological applicability follows from the exact duality and weight sources already matched.','Deligne1973Constants;Deligne1980WeilII','LF-S02','CALC-02','Valid with selfdual coefficients; arbitraryE must be paired withE^∨ instead.')
add(413,[416],[13],'002-035','370–381','point générique … toujours vrai','A generic isomorphism of lisse sheaves on an integral normal scheme extends uniquely. Existence of that generic selfduality is a separate hypothesis.','open on the pages','A','Normal-scheme fundamental-group surjectivity is the exact mechanism; Stacks0BQM states it with full hypotheses. This verifies extension, not the stronger existence reading of the compressed remark.','Stacks0BQM','LF-S03','','The mathematically meaningful extension assertion is established. The uncertain margin cannot be used to remove the selfduality assumption.',confidence='medium')
add(414,[417,420],[13,15],'002-035','379–390,438–445','DE=E(n+ρ)[2n]; χ≡b_n mod2','On a smoothn-fold, D_XE=E^∨(n)[2n]. IfE is selfdual with twistρ, parity and determinant signs reduce to the middle cohomology after pairing degreesi and2n−i.','proof sketched','A','The dualizing complex and proper functional equation are explicit in Deligne1973 §10.5 for curves and in the SGA duality framework. The paired-degree argument is reproved here.','Deligne1973Constants;Illusie2026SGA5','LF-S02','CALC-02','Valid; the pairing targetQ_ℓ(n) on15 conflicts with the adopted geometric convention and is separately flagged.')
add(415,[421],[17],'002-035','473–483','si n+ρ impair … ε=+1','An alternating q-similitude in dimension2m has determinantq^m. A symmetric pairing in the same weight need not have positive normalized determinant.','stated without proof','E','Classical symplectic determinant identity. Deligne’s weight theorems do not replace the alternating-polarization premise.','Deligne1974WeilI','LF-S02','CALC-03','Valid for the polarized alternating case; matrixF=[[0,p],[1,0]],B=diag(1,p) checks failure of the symmetric generalization.')
add(416,[418,422],[15,17],'002-035','423–445,473–483','ξ=t^{χ/2}L; ε′=(-1)^{e_1}','The ±1 multiplicities refer to normalized Frobenius, and a negative sign at a fixed point constrains zero/pole order parity. Half powers require a chosen square-root coordinate.','proof sketched','E','Elementary rational-function reciprocity and paired eigenvalues; the P² case is a complete exact test. No source was found identifying an additional theorem behind the unnormalized shorthand.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S02','CALC-04; CALC-10','Valid with normalization. P² has a central pole and sign−1, so a universal central-zero inference would be false.')
add(417,[423],[19,25,61],'002-035','511–532,665–698','R∞f=R_*f−R_!f','The virtual difference is represented byCone(RΓ_c→RΓ); it fits into the corresponding exact triangle and has the compactification description on61.','proof sketched','A','Localization/duality is part of the SGA framework; Stacks09XP and014D give exact triangle conventions. Wildeshaus2004/2006 is a later motivic comparison, not an identification of categories.','Stacks09XP;Stacks014D;Wildeshaus2006Boundary','LF-S03','CALC-06','Established ℓ-adically. The object must be distinguished from a mere difference of cohomological dimensions.')
add(418,[424],[19,21],'002-035','511–532,561–591','L_c(1/qt)=A(t)δ_c(-t)^χ L_c(t)','For smooth separated finite-typeX and lisseE withE^∨≃E(ρ), putq=p^{n+ρ} andA(t)=L∞(1/(qt))^{-1}; the written corrected nonproper equation follows.','proof sketched','A','Grothendieck duality/trace formalism and Deligne1973 §10 give the established mechanism; the determinant algebra is independently derived in proof_notes.md.','Grothendieck1964Lefschetz;Deligne1973Constants','LF-S03','CALC-04','Valid without the separate resolution/type assertions; A¹ andG_m certify the boundary factors.')
add(419,[425],[21],'002-035','561–579','type≤τ+n−1; poids≤ρ+2n','The page proposes a boundary type bound under resolution and Weil assumptions; its undefined “type” cannot be replaced by a modern weight invariant without reconstruction.','open on the pages','F','Searched SGA/WeilII/boundary-motive literature. Deligne1980 §3.3 supplies precise mixed-cohomology weight bounds, and Wildeshaus §6 supplies boundary duality, but neither identifies the text’s unspecified type predicate.','Deligne1980WeilII;Wildeshaus2006Boundary','LF-S03','','Exact statement not identifiable from the supplied definition. This is not a claim that no boundary weight theorem exists.',confidence='low')
add(420,[426],[21,27],'002-035','580–591,736–766','χ_!=χ_*; δ_!δ_*=q^χ','Under selfduality, χ_c=χ_* and δ_cδ_*=q^χ; consequentlyχ∞=0 andδ∞=q^χδ_c^{-2}.','proof sketched','E','Formal consequences of the established duality; matched to Deligne1973 §10.5 and independently checked.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S03','CALC-04','Valid with consistent alternating determinant conventions.')
add(421,[427],[23],'002-035','617–636','h_!^i; β_i','A virtual weight decomposition gives its determinant as a product of pure-weight determinants with virtual multiplicities. Odd-weight sign positivity additionally needs polarization.','proof sketched','C','WeilII establishes mixed ℓ-adic weight filtrations, including §3.4.1, but it does not supply an unconditional decomposition in the unspecified motivic category used in the shorthand.','Deligne1980WeilII','LF-S02','','The realization-level determinant calculation is valid; the exact motivic type ofh_!^i remains unspecified.',confidence='medium')
add(422,[423],[25,61],'002-035','679–698','à vérifier si1ou−1','For the cohomological coneC∞, D C∞(E)=C∞(DE)[-1]; selfduality on a smoothn-fold yields the2n−1 shift.','open on the pages','B','Stacks014D fixes the cone convention; Wildeshaus Theorem6.1 independently exhibits the same2n−1 shift in his motivic convention with resolution hypothesis. The formal dual-triangle proof resolves the ℓ-adic shift here.','Stacks014D;Wildeshaus2006Boundary','LF-S03','CALC-06','The minus-one answer is proved for the selected cone convention; ink remains undecided.')
