add(428,[434],[33],'002-035','884–888','D(i_*E)=i_*checkE(1)','For a smooth curve and lisseE on a dense open, D(j_*E)=j_*E^∨(1)[2]; the class identity forgets the even shift.','stated without proof','A','Deligne1973 §§10.5–10.7 is the exact curve duality/local-cohomology comparison.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S03','','Valid as a class identity; literal derived equality requires[2].')
add(429,[434],[33,35],'002-035','896–947','L*checkE(1/pt)=(-t)^χ δ L*E(t)','The curve middle-extension L-function satisfies the displayed two-object equation, and the selfdual equation hasq=p^{ρ+1}.','proof sketched','A','Grothendieck’s trace formula and curve duality yield the equation; Deligne1973 §10.5 gives the published counterpart.','Grothendieck1964Lefschetz;Deligne1973Constants','LF-S01','CALC-02','The positiveχ exponent is correct after inversion. It should not be flagged as a sign error.')
add(430,[435,436],[35],'002-035','950–977','Q=Coker(i_*E→i_*E″)','Underived extension of an exact sequence has finite-support cokernelQ; L(E)=L(E′)L(E″)/L(Q), with analogous χ subtraction and δ division, using degree-correct local factors.','proof sketched','E','Standard long exact sequence of invariants; Deligne1973 §10.7 supplies local complexes. The example and all determinant signs are computed here.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','CALC-07; CALC-08','Valid correction formula. Deleted R¹-kernel description agrees with the connecting map.')
add(431,[435],[35],'002-035','966–967','Q … points oùE″ ramifié','The support ofQ need not lie in the ramification locus ofE″: a nontrivial tame unipotent extension with unramified endpoints hasQ≠0.','false as stated','E','Exact invariants obstruction is classical. Deligne1980 §3.4.9 explains why the mixed counterexample does not refute a geometrically semisimple pure setting.','Deligne1973Constants;Deligne1980WeilII','LF-S05','CALC-07','Literal support claim refuted. Correct support bound is the locus where taking invariants fails for the exact sequence, contained in the middle representation’s ramification locus.')
add(432,[441],[35],'002-035','959–963','R¹i_*E′','For the literal generic-point inclusion, R¹i_*Q_ℓ is not constructible globally; its local inertia cohomology is nonzero at every closed point. A fixed dense openj gives the finite-type derived direct image.','corrected by himself later','B','Deligne1973 §10.7 computes the local inertia cohomology. The source deletes the R¹ expression rather than asserting its global constructibility.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','','The generic-direct-image constructibility warning is an independent scope check, not a false theorem expressly asserted by the author.')
add(433,[449],[37],'036-070','20','pas de construction locale … ne commutent pas à l’extension étale','The global-composition-factor recipe is rejected as insufficiently local; the new construction uses local decomposition and inertia groups.','corrected by himself later','C','Modern Weil–Deligne local theory in Deligne1973 §8 gives the appropriate local replacement. No exact published counterexample to the author’s rejected global recipe was located; the manuscript supplies no worked example.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','','The withdrawal is documentary certain; its exact illustrative counterexample is not reconstructed as authorial text.',confidence='medium')
add(434,[450],[39],'036-070','42–46','E^U,(E/E^U)^U,…','IfU◁D acts unipotently on finite-dimensional characteristic-zeroV, iteratedU-fixed spaces give aD-stable filtration withU-trivial graded factors.','proof sketched','E','Classical unipotent-group dévissage; Deligne1973 Theorem8.2 supplies quasi-unipotence for the local ℓ-adic application.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','','Independently proved using the unipotent algebraic closure and normality ofU. Normality is essential.')
add(435,[450,451],[41],'036-070','76–89','moyenne; 1/N','FiniteI/U averaging in characteristic0 defines an exact invariant functor, hence an additiveK₀ map to representations ofD/I after unipotent dévissage.','proof sketched','E','Maschke averaging and local quasi-unipotence give the exact setting. The tensor strengthening is disproved by theC₂ sign example.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','CALC-07','Valid additive construction; not a tensor functor.')
add(436,[450],[41,43],'036-070','83–89,116–122','indépendant deU','The additive class is unchanged after replacingU by a smallerD-normal finite-index subgroup; scalar extension and the stated continuity are compatible.','proof sketched','E','Dévissage plus transitivity of finite-group invariants proves the assertion. The quotient-category map labelledrestriction is inflation.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','','Valid under the page’s finite-dimensional characteristic-zero hypotheses; not arbitrary infinite-dimensional averaging.')
add(437,[450],[45,47],'036-070','146–163,195','Tr(g,E^♮)=1/N ΣTr(gh,E)','The average overI/U computes the quotient trace and is independent of Frobenius lift after passing through theD-stableU-trivial filtration.','proof sketched','E','Classical finite-group trace averaging; Deligne1973 §8 is the precise local setting, not a substitute for the manuscript’s filtration proof.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','CALC-07','Valid. The ambiguousg∈I/U must be checked againstD/U in the scan.')
add(438,[452],[47],'036-070','199–211','i_!E_U+Σj_x*Eη^♮(x)','Replacing the finitely many boundary stalks by their averaged classes defines a constructibleK₀ class independent of the chosen dense open of lissity.','proof sketched','E','For an added unramified point the averaged class is the original stalk, so the two extension formulas agree; this is an independent direct proof.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','','Valid as a virtual class. The overloaded notationEη(x) must not be carried intoα without distinction.')
add(439,[453],[49,51],'036-070','233–266,289–328','μ=α(E)^∨−α(checkE)(1)','The virtual duality defect equals the displayed difference ofα terms, whereα=V^♮−V^I and geometric twists are fixed.','proof sketched','B','Deligne1973 §§8.2,10.7 supplies the Weil–Deligne/inertia complex permitting an exact comparison. The formula is independently derived here after resolving the notation collision.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','CALC-07; CALC-08','Valid repaired notation; under the stated local categoryμ=0 inK₀, althoughα need not vanish.')
add(440,[453,457],[51,55],'036-070','315–328,448','μ est additif','The defectμ is additive inV. Since everyV has a filtration withU-trivial factors andμ vanishes on these,μ vanishes identically in the stated quasi-unipotent category.','proof sketched','B','This is an independent consequence of the page’s proof and Deligne1973 local model. It is not presented as a located later paper specifically discussing these unpublished symbols.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','CALC-07','Additivity is asserted on the page; vanishing is our proved implication. The author’s warning about splitα factors remains valid.')
add(441,[453],[51],'036-070','289–328','μ(checkE)=−checkμ(E)(1)','Dualizingα-formulas gives the antisymmetry law, and underE^∨≃E(ρ), μ=α^∨−α(ρ+1).','proof sketched','E','Direct dual/twist calculation in the local representation ring, consistent with Deligne1973 §10.7.','Deligne1973Constants','LF-S05','CALC-07; CALC-08','Valid as a formal identity and compatible withμ=0.')
add(442,[454],[53,55],'036-070','363–404,431–447','L_μ = L_{α^∨}/L_{α(checkE)}','The denominator must evaluate atp^-1t, and atp^{-(ρ+1)}t in the selfdual case. Some subsequent lines lose that factor.','false as stated','E','The page’s precedingμ identity plus the geometric twist convention determines the correction. Published conventions in Deligne1973/Laumon1987 agree.','Deligne1973Constants;Laumon1987Fourier','LF-S05','CALC-08','Literal dropped-twist versions fail. Scan review must determine whether the omission is ink or transcription.')
add(443,[492],[55],'036-070','450–456','calculerα,μ,λ; valeurs absolues','Determine local degeneration factors and eigenvalue absolute values, beyond the formal averaging formula.','open on the pages','B','Deligne1980 Theorem1.8.4 and Remark1.8.8 give local monodromy purity for pure lisse sheaves on curves over finite fields; §§3.3–3.4 add mixed weights. This answers a precise curve realization, not every unspecified motivic generalization.','Deligne1980WeilII','LF-S02','','Established in the stated equal-characteristic curve setting; individual local polynomials still depend on the actual representation.')
add(444,[455],[55,59],'036-070','454,538','calculerχ; représentations d’Artin','The modified extension hasχ^♮=rχ_c(Ū)−Σ_deg(x)Swan_x(V)+Σ_deg(x)dim(V_x^♮), with both sums over missing closed points.','open on the pages','A','Raynaud’s Bourbaki286 §3 states Grothendieck’s Euler-characteristic formula (talkFeb1965, publication1966); the finite-support adjustment is formal. Laumon1987(3.1.5.3) gives its conductor form.','Raynaud1965Euler;Laumon1987Fourier','LF-S06','','Established with degree conventions. The page’s Artin-representation hint is not itself a complete proof.')
